{
  "_": "Brief 5 loot: which authored piece each opponent drops and the player slot it fills. Sources are parts.py/items outputs in the shared unscaled rest space (build-warrior.mjs contract: extras.material/slot + extras.bone or skin weights). `slots`/`names` pick meshes out of a shared file; `unscale` names the BUILD proportion table a piece was cut under. Slots: Helmet, Crest, Body, Arms, Gloves, Greaves, Boots. `layer`: 'replace' hides the player's own draws in that slot (a helm hides the hair, a tunic the tunic, boots the sandals); 'over' is worn on top of them (greaves over bare shins, a plate over a wrap). Body = the tunic and what hangs on it (baldric, belt, buckle, studs, collar) \u2014 kilt/skirt/hose are leg cloth with no paperdoll slot and stay the player's; wraps are the Arms item where an opponent wears nothing over them. A tunic's material becomes Gambeson_<opponent> (his own linen bake) \u2014 see build-warrior.mjs. A `replace` piece must cover at least 80 % of the player's own draws in that slot (tests/loot.test.ts): the Pitborn's chest was a rag sash at 26 % and is not loot \u2014 he wears no tunic by design (parts.py KIT `bare`).",
